**K16 is one precise atom on one prototype. It is not the unique structural gap of the programme.** Neither a finite census nor one cofinal family supplies an all-degree covering theorem. The single most valuable next object is a **certificate-bearing receiver atlas**: an explicit source-to-receiver map for every branch being charged, with an honest UNASSIGNED output. Its first finite test is already available: the sharpened 296-row cohort, its 132 coarse keys, and its higher-depth collisions. This should precede a large class sweep. The finite Moh closure can continue alongside it.

